Z||000000||wxxo||07-19-2000||11:45 AM||||ok wrench heads got a question for yall. how hard is is to switch trannys?? im talkin about changing my broken four speed for another four speed. this is in an 86 v6 se. will i have to drop the cradle out or is there a way to just take the tranny out and bolt the new one in?? tia||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||07-19-2000||12:01 PM||||Yep thats it! replace the axle seals in the new tranny and you'll need the little ball thingys that the cables attach to for the shift cables. just pull your old one out and toss in the new one.. I went from a 3:65 86 4spd to an 84 4:10 4spd. Clutchs are the same the throwout bearings are the same. the speedo sending units are the same. I had my whole box gone throught and bearings replaced and a synchro or two replaced so i'd only have to do it once... figures I'd trade the car a month later... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||07-19-2000||05:18 PM||||wxxo... Check Ed Parks' Fiero Factory page. Seems like he had a write up, describing how too get the clutch (therefore, the tranny) out, without dropping the cradle. Seems like you had to drop the left side, and just loosen the right side.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||07-19-2000||06:27 PM||||I'd say it's easier to take the cradle out than trying to do it in car. It's an afternoon to get it out and an afternoon back in, plus the disconnect. Take the axels off first and you won't have to do the rear alignment.<P>Why not put in a 5 speed while your at it?<P>my $.02.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||07-20-2000||03:30 AM||||How hard is it to do? Very<BR>Then again, is there really anything mechanically to do on a Fiero that ISNT hard to do? Nope! lol......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
